## 3. Driving the save panel (the expensive part)
# - The panel is NOT in Logic's process: it is "Open and Save Panel Service (Logic Pro)"
#   (com.apple.appkit.xpc.openAndSavePanelService). Logic's AX tree proxies it (reads + AXPress work),
#   but CGEvents posted to Logic's pid never reach it; HID-tap events go to whatever is frontmost
#   (one attempt typed a path + Return into the terminal). Post events to the panel service's pid.
# - Go To Folder: ⌘⇧G (to the panel pid) opens an AXSheet with one AXTextField; AXValue write + ⏎ navigates.
# - Save As field: an AXValue write shows in the field but the panel keeps its old name. Click the field
#   (CGEvent to the panel pid), set AXSelectedTextRange to everything, type the name as unicode key events.
#   The panel has a second AXTextField (search, with search/cancel children): pick the one with no children.
# - Save: AXPress works most runs; in some runs AXEnabled read false while the button was visibly active
#   (Margot clicked it by hand once; a HID click with a Logic-frontmost guard is the coded fallback).
$ /tmp/rb export all .../out/clean1.mid
   133 ms press File > Export > All MIDI Tracks as MIDI File…  (enabled=true)
   133 ms AXPress -> ok
  1530 ms posting events to panel service pid 13991
  1710 ms click AXTextField at 798,157
  2050 ms keystroke 'g' cmd=true opt=false shift=true ctrl=false
  2558 ms Go To sheet open
  2732 ms field set via AXValue
  2887 ms keystroke '⏎'
  3234 ms Go To sheet closed; where = out
  3656 ms click AXTextField at 798,157
  4351 ms field typed; reads 'clean1.mid'
  4738 ms press Save (AX) -> 0
  4956 ms file written: .../out/clean1.mid
export round trip 4846 ms            (second clean run: 4521 ms; selection run: 4424 ms)

## 4. Region identity
# Margot renamed Track 1 to "hello :P" (the rename hit the track): every exported track became "hello :P".
# Margot then renamed region 2 (bars 3–4.5) to "second":
track 1: name "hello :P"  instrument "hello :P"
track 2: name "second"    instrument "hello :P"    <- SMF track name (meta 03) = REGION name
track 3: name "hello :P"  instrument "hello :P"    <- meta 04 (instrument name) = Logic TRACK name
track 4: name "hello :P"  instrument "hello :P"
track 5: name "hello :P"  instrument "hello :P"
# A region with the default name exports under the track name, so unnamed regions are told apart by
# start tick + order only. Naming a region before the round trip gives a stable handle.

